# `nx format:check` passes files to prettier as explicit patterns and prettier
# exits 2 on an explicitly-named symlink, so the two symlinks to AGENTS.md are
# named here.
CLAUDE.md
GEMINI.md

# A `git worktree` under the checkout is a second copy of every project, and
# Nx's graph reads it as a duplicate: `MultipleProjectsWithSameNameError: be-01
# is defined in multiple locations`, which fails `run-many` before a single
# target runs. The convention here is `.worktrees/<name>` (AGENTS.md's agent
# loop audit), so the directory is excluded rather than each worktree.
#
# Nx does not read `.gitignore` or `.git/info/exclude`, which is why the same
# directory has to be named here as well as there. Git's side is `.gitignore`'s
# `.worktrees/`: without it a lane's worktree is untracked, and
# `bin/h2puni-gate.sh` refuses a tree that is dirty after its checkout (exit 65).
.worktrees
